\section{Masked functions}{

Two exports share their names with functions of the base distribution:
\code{\link[=search]{search()}} with \code{\link[base:search]{base::search()}} and \code{\link[=update]{update()}} with \code{\link[stats:update]{stats::update()}}.
After \code{library(cttiR)} the unqualified names refer to cttiR, so
\code{update(fit, ...)} no longer updates a fitted model. Either call cttiR
without attaching it (\code{cttiR::project()}, \code{cttiR::search()}), as the
README and vignettes do, or qualify the masked functions
(\code{base::search()}, \code{stats::update()}). \code{\link[=update_knowledge]{update_knowledge()}} is the same
function as \code{\link[=update]{update()}} under a name that masks nothing.
}

